    "aboutText": "Shiv Shringar Sewa Samiti is a group of young devotees who serve at Prachin Hanuman Mandir, East Azad Nagar. Every single day we adorn the Shivling and Mata Rani with flowers, sandalwood, bhasm, garments and ornaments, followed by bhajan, kirtan and aarti.\n\nOn festivals and auspicious days we prepare a special shringar — Mahakal, the nine forms of Durga during Navratri, Shiv Parivar, Krishna's Nauka Vihar on Janmashtami and many more. We also organise Rudrabhishek, prasad seva and group pilgrimages.",
